{"units": [{"id": "engrapho-quote5", "translation": "These things are not written on tablets."}, {"id": "engye-orth1", "translation": "surety, pledge"}, {"id": "engye-def1", "translation": "surety, pledge"}, {"id": "engye-quote1", "translation": "And will he give me a pledge for all time?"}, {"id": "engythen-orth1", "translation": "near, from nearby"}, {"id": "engythen-def1", "translation": "near, from nearby"}, {"id": "engythen-quote1", "translation": "These things are near such griefs."}, {"id": "engythen-quote2", "translation": "He himself was present near the dying man."}, {"id": "engythen-quote3", "translation": "For you do not see from nearby."}, {"id": "engys-orth1", "translation": "near"}, {"id": "engys-def1", "translation": "near"}, {"id": "engys-note1", "translation": "Concerning kinship"}, {"id": "engys-quote1", "translation": "For already the fully armed army of the Argives is advancing near."}, {"id": "engys-quote2", "translation": "Standing near the tomb."}, {"id": "engys-quote3", "translation": "Standing near."}, {"id": "engys-quote4", "translation": "May he not be a shield-companion to me nor near."}, {"id": "engys-quote5", "translation": "Those near to Zeus."}, {"id": "engys-quote6", "translation": "Claiming to be nearest in kinship."}, {"id": "egeiro-orth1", "translation": "to wake, rouse"}, {"id": "egeiro-def1", "translation": "to wake, rouse"}, {"id": "egeiro-def2", "translation": "to be awake"}, {"id": "egeiro-note1", "translation": "Thus Porson for ἐγρήγορον [awake]."}, {"id": "egeiro-quote1", "translation": "He roused another relay of the fire-messenger."}, {"id": "egeiro-quote2", "translation": "Wake, wake her too, and I will wake you."}, {"id": "egeiro-quote3", "translation": "Until I rouse the bridegrooms to be gracious."}, {"id": "egeiro-quote4", "translation": "I establish myself as a waking guardian of the land."}, {"id": "egeiro-quote5", "translation": "The ruin of the dead would be awake."}, {"id": "egeiro-word1", "translation": "awake"}, {"id": "enkathiemi-orth1", "translation": "to send in, implant"}, {"id": "enkathiemi-def1", "translation": "to send in, implant"}, {"id": "enkathiemi-quote1", "translation": "For father Zeus implants these oracles in Loxias."}, {"id": "enkataskepto-orth1", "translation": "to fall upon, strike"}, {"id": "enkataskepto-def1", "translation": "to fall upon, strike"}, {"id": "enkataskepto-quote1", "translation": "Of evils which a god hurled upon the Persians."}, {"id": "enkatillopto-orth1", "translation": "to mock, sneer at"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-def1", "translation": "to mock, sneer at"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-note1", "translation": "(in Pollux 10, 20)"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-note2", "translation": "where the manuscripts have εὐ κατιλλώψας [having mocked well]."}, {"id": "enkatillopto-note3", "translation": "Hesychius: ἐγκατιλλώψαι [to mock]: ἐγκαταμυκτηρίσαι [to sneer at]."}, {"id": "enkatillopto-quote1", "translation": "Having greatly mocked you."}, {"id": "enkatillopto-quote2", "translation": "The keeper of the stall, having mocked,"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-quote3", "translation": "having mocked well"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-quote4", "translation": "to mock"}, {"id": "enkatillopto-quote5", "translation": "to sneer at"}, {"id": "enkeleuo-orth1", "translation": "to command, urge on"}, {"id": "enkeleuo-def1", "translation": "to command, urge on"}, {"id": "enkeleuo-quote1", "translation": "Do not urge too much."}, {"id": "enkoneo-orth1", "translation": "to hasten, accomplish quickly"}, {"id": "enkoneo-def1", "translation": "to hasten, accomplish quickly"}, {"id": "enkoneo-quote1", "translation": "Hasten back along the road by which you came."}, {"id": "enkoteo-orth1", "translation": "to be angry at"}, {"id": "enkoteo-def1", "translation": "to be angry at"}, {"id": "enkoteo-quote1", "translation": "And to be angry at the slayers."}, {"id": "enkotys-orth1", "translation": "angry, wrathful"}, {"id": "enkotys-def1", "translation": "angry, wrathful"}, {"id": "enkotys-note1", "translation": "Hermann conjectured that it should be restored for коτος [wrath], which is read in Hesychius (s.v. ἐναροφόρος [bearing spoils]) with a lacuna of two letters."}, {"id": "enkotys-quote1", "translation": "Wrathful hatred."}, {"id": "enkotys-quote2", "translation": "The wrathful hounds of my mother."}, {"id": "enkotys-quote3", "translation": "wrathful"}, {"id": "enkotys-quote4", "translation": "wrath"}, {"id": "enkotys-quote5", "translation": "bearing spoils"}, {"id": "enkouras-orth1", "translation": "painted tablet"}, {"id": "enkouras-def1", "translation": "painted tablet"}, {"id": "enkouras-note1", "translation": "(in Hesychius s.v. κουράς [shearing]), where, since ΕΝΚΟΥΡΑΔΙ was written, Hesychius says it was doubted whether this was ἐν κουράδι [in a shearing] or ἐγκουράδι [in a painted tablet]: on which see the note."}, {"id": "enkouras-quote1", "translation": "shearing"}, {"id": "enkouras-quote2", "translation": "in a shearing"}, {"id": "enkouras-quote3", "translation": "in a painted tablet"}, {"id": "enkouras-word1", "translation": "ΕΝΚΟΥΡΑΔΙ"}, {"id": "enkrates-orth1", "translation": "strong, mighty"}, {"id": "enkrates-def1", "translation": "strong, mighty"}, {"id": "enkrates-quote1", "translation": "With mighty strength."}, {"id": "encheiridios-orth1", "translation": "held in the hand"}, {"id": "encheiridios-def1", "translation": "held in the hand"}, {"id": "encheiridios-quote1", "translation": "With these suppliant branches held in the hand, wreathed with wool."}, {"id": "encheo-orth1", "translation": "to pour in"}, {"id": "encheo-def1", "translation": "to pour in"}, {"id": "encheo-note1", "translation": "Thus Canter for ἐκχέας [having poured out]."}, {"id": "encheo-quote1", "translation": "Having poured vinegar and oil into the same vessel."}, {"id": "encheo-word1", "translation": "having poured out"}, {"id": "enchlio-orth1", "translation": "to insult, mock"}, {"id": "enchlio-def1", "translation": "to insult, mock"}, {"id": "enchlio-quote1", "translation": "You mock the Greeks too much."}, {"id": "enchlio-quote2", "translation": "In your toils they mock greatly."}, {"id": "enchos-orth1", "translation": "spear"}, {"id": "enchos-def1", "translation": "spear"}, {"id": "enchos-quote1", "translation": "Upright spears."}, {"id": "enchos-quote2", "translation": "A spear weighted at the butt."}, {"id": "enchorios-orth1", "translation": "native, of the land"}, {"id": "enchorios-def1", "translation": "native, of the land"}, {"id": "enchorios-quote1", "translation": "At the altars of the native gods."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote2", "translation": "The native gods."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote3", "translation": "Of the native gods."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote4", "translation": "Of the native divinities."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote5", "translation": "And he is very much a native."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote6", "translation": "For you are more like Libyan women than native ones."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote7", "translation": "Send companions and guides of the native land."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote8", "translation": "Calling together the native people."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote9", "translation": "Well are the affairs of the natives."}, {"id": "enchorios-quote10", "translation": "To the native protectors."}, {"id": "enchoros-orth1", "translation": "native"}, {"id": "enchoros-def1", "translation": "native"}, {"id": "enchoros-note1", "translation": "Thus Hermann for λαῶν ἐν χώρῳ [of the people in the land]."}, {"id": "enchoros-quote1", "translation": "Of the native people."}, {"id": "enchoros-word1", "translation": "of the people in the land"}, {"id": "ego-orth1", "translation": "I"}, {"id": "ego-def1", "translation": "I"}, {"id": "ego-def2", "translation": "ἐγώ [I] combined with γε [indeed] coalesces into one word ἔγωγε [I indeed], and likewise the dative ἔμοιγε [to me indeed]"}]}